# ── Build outputs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `node build.js` writes both of these from js/ and css/. Neither is committed:
# together they are ~12MB that changes on EVERY art or code edit, which would
# bloat the history far faster than the sources themselves. The Pages workflow
# rebuilds aegis-protocol.html on each deploy, so the single-file download is
# always available from the site — just never out of the repository.
aegis-protocol.html
aegis-artifact.html

# ── Art generation ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The rendered plates are reproducible from artgen/krea_jobs.py, and the packed
# js/artpack.js IS committed, so the caches are pure intermediate state.
# krea2-turbo/ is a ~34GB model checkout (fetch with artgen/dl_krea.py) — never commit it.
artgen/cache/
artgen/cache_krea/
artgen/krea2-turbo/
artgen/*.safetensors
artgen/*.bin

# ── Local scratch ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
_*.js
_*.json
_*.md
!docs/**
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Python ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# ── Editors ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# The canon pack (v0.2.0) is its own repository with its own publishing
# workflow. It is the SOURCE for the game copy, not part of the game site;
# publishing it is a separate decision the owner makes deliberately.
lore/
